  {
    "id": "AC-001",
    "criterion": "An explicit X.Y.Z or callisto@X.Y.Z request resolves to that one semantic version. In source=auto only a confirmed not-found release asset may fall back to the registry package with that identical version; authorization, rate-limit, 5xx, timeout, transport, malformed response, checksum, attestation, extraction, or version failures are terminal. source=release and source=registry never switch sources. If the selected immutable source cannot supply and verify the exact version, setup exits nonzero and never invokes unpinned cargo install --git.",
    "is_error_case": true
  },
  {
    "id": "AC-002",
    "criterion": "latest is resolved once to an immutable product version before installation and that resolved version is printed. Fallback between release assets and the registry retains that exact resolved version; it never asks each source independently for its latest version and never falls back to a branch.",
    "is_error_case": true
  },
  {
    "id": "AC-003",
    "criterion": "source=local is the only mode that builds the current checkout, requires a Callisto workspace, rejects an exact release-version input, and reports the checkout commit and built CLI version. Merely running inside the Callisto monorepo cannot override source=auto, release, or registry.",
    "is_error_case": true
  },
  {
    "id": "AC-004",
    "criterion": "Release-asset installation supports exactly aarch64-apple-darwin, x86_64-unknown-linux-musl, and aarch64-unknown-linux-musl. Unsupported operating systems and architectures fail with an actionable diagnostic rather than selecting a Linux or amd64 default.",
    "is_error_case": true
  },
  {
    "id": "AC-005",
    "criterion": "Before extraction or PATH modification, the commit-pinned setup helper independently anchors the allowed `orin-dx/callisto` repository and release-build workflow path, then consumes SPEC-RELEASE-PRODUCT-MODEL-001's versioned public `callisto-release-metadata.json` contract and requires its repository/workflow claims to match that allowlist. It verifies metadata and the selected payload against the exact product tag, source commit, SHA256SUMS, immutable workflow commit, and GitHub artifact attestations, then requires the installed binary to report the resolved version. Downloaded metadata can narrow or bind policy but can never authorize its own repository or workflow trust root.",
    "is_error_case": true
  },
  {
    "id": "AC-006",
    "criterion": "The resolver has table-driven action tests covering every source mode, both exact-version spellings, latest pinning, local-checkout precedence, each supported platform mapping, every unsupported-platform error, release-to-registry fallback with the same pinned version, and proof that no failure path executes an unpinned Git installation.",
    "is_error_case": true
  },
  {
    "id": "AC-007",
    "criterion": "One checked-in `.github` helper owns source resolution, ProductReleaseId-equivalent tag/version parsing, asset mapping, checksum verification, metadata verification, and attestation verification for setup-callisto and setup-callisto-wasm. The helper consumes the release contract and cannot derive release rosters or names from mutable checkout configuration; any artifact-type-specific divergence is explicit and tested.",
    "is_error_case": true
  }
]

